{"name":"Astral Nomad","hex":"#203943","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"astral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to or resembling the stars; starry.","Relating to an aster."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being from the astral plane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astral"},{"term":"nomad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a society or class who herd animals from pasture to pasture with no fixed home.","Synonym of wanderer: an itinerant person."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of nomadic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nomad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nomad","blocks":[{"text":"Nomads are communities without fixed habitation who regularly move to and from areas. Such groups include hunter-gatherers, pastoral nomads, tinkers and trader nomads. In the twentieth century, the population of nomadic pastoral tribes slowly decreased, reaching an estimated 30–40 million nomads in the world as of 1995."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg/330px-Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomad","wikidata":"Q128393"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg/500px-Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg/1280px-Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563.jpg/500px-Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_NGM-v31-p563